# Cache rules, for hosts that read them.
#
# Cloudflare Pages honours this file. GitHub Pages ignores it entirely and itch.io serves a zip, so
# shipping it to all three costs nothing and takes effect wherever it can. See
# docs/decisions/0008-the-shell-sidecars.md.
#
# THE SHELL IS NEVER SERVED FROM CACHE WITHOUT ASKING. GitHub Pages sends index.html with
# `Cache-Control: max-age=600` and gives you no way to change it, which is what stranded the
# predecessor's installed app on the previous build for ten minutes after every deploy. Where the
# header IS ours to set, it says the honest thing: revalidate the shell every time.
#
# `no-cache` is NOT `no-store`. It lets the browser keep the single-file bundle and send
# `If-None-Match`, so an unchanged build costs a 304 rather than a full re-download on mobile data.
#
# ⚠️ Every rule here is correct on ANY host, which is deliberate: if production ever moves, this
# file makes it strictly fresher and never staler. Nothing below is staging-specific — keep it that
# way, or this becomes a setting that silently changes meaning when the host does.
#
# ⚠️ `/sw.js` matters most. A cached service worker is a cached DECISION about how everything else
# is served, and it outlives the tab that installed it.
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache
